# AI HR Candidate Matcher — Phase 1 Implementation Plan

Extend the existing RAG application into a production-ready, deterministic **AI HR Resume & Candidate Matching Assistant**.

This plan preserves all existing RAG and general chat capabilities while introducing a job-isolated candidate screening workflow with skill normalization, hybrid evidence retrieval, FlashRank cross-encoder reranking, LLM evidence extraction, deterministic scoring math, SQLite persistence, and a dedicated HR Dashboard UI.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Deterministic Scoring Architecture**: Candidate qualification percentage scores will **NOT** be generated directly by LLMs. Instead, LLMs will perform structured fact & evidence extraction from candidate resumes, and application code in Python will apply configurable deterministic weights:
> - **Required Skills**: 40%
> - **Relevant Experience**: 25%
> - **Project Relevance**: 15%
> - **Preferred Skills**: 10%
> - **Education**: 5%
> - **Domain Fit**: 5%

> [!NOTE]
> **Zero Regression & Component Reuse**: We reuse existing components without duplication:
> - Document Loaders (`loader_factory.py`)
> - Text Splitter & Embeddings (`sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`)
> - ChromaDB Vector Store (`chroma_db`) & BM25 Keyword Search (`BM25Retriever`)
> - Reranking (`FlashRank`)
> - Groq LLM Provider (`ChatGroq`)
> - JWT Authentication (`app/api/deps.py`)

---

## Open Questions

1. **Database Backend**: The specification allows SQLite or PostgreSQL. We propose using **SQLite** (`hr_db.py` in `app/db/`) via SQLAlchemy, keeping zero extra setup requirement for local development while remaining 100% compatible with PostgreSQL. Is SQLite preferred for local dev? *(Recommended: SQLite via SQLAlchemy)*.
2. **Backward Compatibility**: Should we maintain legacy single-job endpoints (`/hr/upload-jd`, `/hr/upload-resumes`, `/hr/leaderboard`) alongside the new job-isolated routes (`/hr/jobs/{job_id}/...`)? *(Recommended: Yes, wrap legacy endpoints to use default active `job_id`)*.

